<title>FRANCE: Canal Plus sees 1997 breakeven.</title>
<headline>Canal Plus sees 1997 breakeven.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French pay television group Canal Plus expects 1997 results to break even, company finance director Laurent Perpere told financial analysts on Monday, reaffirming earlier forecasts.</p>
<p>In 1996, Canal Plus had net attributable profit of 741 million francs, up 11.3 percent. But in April, it will merge with Nethold.</p>
<p>Canal Plus estimates that cumulative operating losses of Nethold will total 1.7 billion francs over three years before attaining breakeven.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
